ystem\n| Special topic – Exercise 1. Soil composition\nWeek 3 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis– Soil texture (Ex. 2)\n| Mineral fraction and water (Ex. 3)\n| Roots/Vessels & Pesticides\nWeek 4 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis\n| Team skills exercise (for example, Drawing together)\n| Special topic – Exercise 4. Observing soil organic matter\nWeek 5 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis\n| Team fun exercise (for example, String)\n| Special topic – Exercise 5.", "chunk_id": "74dcf6b2017d54d1a257d465a3dc1d22cd609b9b", "relevance_topic": "phosphorus", "relevance_topics": [{"topic": "phosphorus", "score": 0.5394}, {"topic": "pest_disease_management", "score": 0.5329}, {"topic": "soil_moisture_irrigation", "score": 0.531}], "semantic_score": 0.5394, "lexical_bonus": 0.0, "low_value_penalty": 0.0, "relevance_score": 0.5394}
{"source_file": "/content/drive/MyDrive/Agronomy_Data_Source/ca8167en.pdf", "source_name": "ca8167en.pdf", "page_start": 70, "page_end": 70, "section": null, "extraction_method": "pymupdf", "text": "SOIL HEALTH FOR PADDY RICE\nActivities\nWeek 8\nAgro-Ecosystem Analysis\nTeam fun (for example, Drama)\nSpecial topic – Exercise 6.Source of Organic material (Ex. 6)\nWeek 9\nAgro-Ecosystem Analysis\nTeam skills exercise (for example, minitower and bridge)\nReduced Exposure to Pesticides & Pesticide Toxicity\nWeek 10\nAgro-Ecosystem Analysis\nEnergizer exercise (for example, Ballons on leg)\nRelevant exercise on soils and water (Special topics - Exercise. 9 or 10)\nWeek 11\nAgro-Ecosystem Analysis\nBeing a Natural Enemy\nLife cycles: Parasites, Stemborers, and Leaf-folders\nWeek 12\nAgro-Ecosystem Analysis\nMaking kabob\nRats, Snail or other topic\nWeek 13\nAgro-Ecosystem Analysis\nProposal Writing, Workplans, Budget\nCommunity Self-Survey\nWeek 14\nAgro-Ecosystem Analysis\nField Day Planning\nSeed Selection or other Topic\nWeek 15\nPost-test\nField Day/Harvest and Weighing of Field Trials\nClosing Ceremony with Certificates\nPost-FFS\nInform FFS participants of pre- and post-test scores\nMake regular visits to follow-up activities\nPreseason\nand weeks 1-7\n➔\n\n[TABLE 1]\nActivities |\nWeek 8 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis\n| Team fun (for example, Drama)\n| Special topic – Exercise 6.Source of Organic material (Ex. 6)\nWeek 9 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis\n| Team skills exercise (for example, minitower and bridge)\n| Reduced Exposure to Pesticides & Pesticide Toxicity\nWeek 10 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis\n| Energizer exercise (for example, Ballons on leg)\n| Relevant exercise on soils and water (Special topics - Exercise. 9 or 10)\nWeek 11 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis\n| Being a Natural Enemy\n| Life cycles: Parasites, Stemborers, and Leaf-folders\nWeek 12 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis\n| Making kabob\n| Rats, Snail or other topic\nWeek 13 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis\n| Proposal Writing, Workplans, Budget\n| Community Self-Survey\nWeek 14 | Agro-Ecosystem Analysis\n| Field Day Planning\n| Seed Selection or other Topic\nWeek 15 | Post-test\n| Field Day/Harvest and Weighing of Field Trials\n| Closing Ceremony with Certificates\nPost-FFS | Inform FFS participants of pre- and post-test scores\n| Make regular visits to follow-up activities", "chunk_id": "dc26f3a9198186144093aa329d3249dff7dd3f9d", "relevance_topic": "pest_disease_management", "relevance_topics": [{"topic": "pest_disease_management", "score": 0.5444}, {"topic": "soil_ph", "score": 0.5423}, {"topic": "soil_moisture_irrigation", "score": 0.5393}], "semantic_score": 0.5444, "lexical_bonus": 0.036, "low_value_penalty": 0.0, "relevance_score": 0.5804}
{"source_file": "/content/drive/MyDrive/Agronomy_Data_Source/ca8167en.pdf", "source_name": "ca8167en.pdf", "page_start": 73, "page_end": 73, "section": null, "extraction_method": "pymupdf", "text": "REFERENCES\nFAO. 2000. Living Soils: Training for integrated soil management. The FAO Programme for Community IPM in Asia, Bangkok. 101 pp. Available on-line:\nhttps://www.share4dev.info/ffsnet/documents/3144.pdf\nFAO. 2015. Healthy soils are the basis for healthy food production. Food & Agriculture Organization, Rome, Italy. FAO. 2016. Farmer Field School Guidance Document: Planning for quality programmes. Food & Agriculture Organization, Rome, Italy. FAO. 2017a. Soil Organic Carbon: the hidden potential. Food and Agriculture\nOrganization of the United Nations, Rome, Italy. FAO. 2017b. Discovery-based learning on land and water management:\nA practical guide for farmer field schools. Rome, 348 pp. Available on-line: http://www.fao.org/3/a-i6897e.pdf\nGiller, K.E., Misiko, M. & Tittonell, P. 2006. Managing organic resources\nfor soil amendment. Leisa Magazine, 22.4: 16–17. Moldenhauer, K. & Slaton, N. 2001. Rice growth and development. Rice production handbook: 7–14.\n", "chunk_id": "0a6bd5361605450c3051ff763baf2ddfff2ec7ed", "relevance_topic": "phosphorus", "relevance_topics": [{"topic": "phosphorus", "score": 0.6413}, {"topic": "electrical_conductivity", "score": 0.6303}, {"topic": "soil_health", "score": 0.6293}], "semantic_score": 0.6413, "lexical_bonus": 0.012, "low_value_penalty": 0.06, "relevance_score": 0.5933}
